  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty}\\left\\{\\frac{\\sqrt{n+1}+\\sqrt{n+2}+\\ldots+\\sqrt{2 n-1}}{n^{3 / 2}}\\right\\}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}(2 \\sqrt{2}-1)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}(\\sqrt{2}-1)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}(\\sqrt{2}+1)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}(2 \\sqrt{2}+1)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because \\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty \\left[\\frac{\\sqrt{n+1}+\\sqrt{n+2}+\\ldots+\\sqrt{2 n-1}}{n^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right]}$\r\n$=\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty 1}\\left[\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{n}}+\\sqrt{1+\\frac{2}{n}}+\\ldots+\\sqrt{1+\\frac{n-1}{n}}\\right] \\frac{1}{n}$\r\n$=\\lim _{n \\rightarrow \\infty 1} \\sum_{r=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{n} \\sqrt{1+\\frac{r}{n}}$\r\n$=\\int_{0}^{1} \\sqrt{1+x} d x=\\left[\\frac{2}{3}(1+x)^{3 / 2}\\right]_{0}^{1}=\\frac{2}{3}(2 \\sqrt{2}-1)$"
  }
